THE MODIFICATION (2026-10-26, part 6) — the `← Console` exit
------------------------------------------------------------
Added: a `← Console` control in the app panel's authenticated chrome — the
topbar's trailing cluster, on every page — so a person who entered the CRM
through the platform's federated hand-off can return to the console that owns
their identity, from any screen, without editing the address bar.

Reason: `design/CONTRACT.md` §11 requirement 7 makes the exit mandatory for every
module — *"a way back to the console; no trapping, and no module-owned logout that
strands the user"* — and the console's own side of the same table promises "a way
back, always". The two module SPAs that the platform ships (the Workflow Builder
canvas and the Inbox) already carry the control and both build it as

    /console/?realm=<slug>&returnTo=<url-encoded path>

so this is the same URL shape in the fourth codebase, not a fourth shape. The CRM
previously had no console-return control at all: its own sign-in surface is closed
when PLATFORM_CONSOLE_URL is set (§ part 5), so a tenant that wanted out of the
CRM had to edit the URL — trapping, exactly what §11.7 forbids.

WHERE THE REALM COMES FROM. The session, server-side, from the two records this
fork's federation writes — never a constant, and never a value the browser
supplies: the `{realm, id_token}` entry the callback stores for sign-out (part 5),
or the federated identity link `UserSocialAccount(provider_name: 'keycloak',
provider_id: '<realm>|<sub>')` (part 4), which also covers a session established
before the id_token was retained. A session with neither (a stock self-host local
user, the platform operator) gets the realm omitted, which is the documented
fallback: the console's front door asks which workspace rather than the link
guessing one. The realm is validated as a single path segment before it is used.

