THE MODIFICATION (2026-10-28, part 8) — the read-only consent mirror
-------------------------------------------------------------------
Added: five contact fields that are a projection of the platform's consent store
(marketing_optin, dnc, optout_reason, jurisdiction, lawful_basis), a guard that
refuses a tenant-authenticated write to any of them, the platform-only door the
orchestrator's drain writes through, and the controlled withdrawal-reason
vocabulary on optout_reason.

Reason: the platform owns consent. A CRM form, an import, an MCP tool or a
scripted API call that can set `marketing_optin: granted` for somebody who
withdrew is exactly the failure consent tracking exists to prevent, and one
writable copy of the truth is the only way to avoid it. The mirror is therefore
read-only for every tenant-authenticated caller and writable only through
POST /api/v1/platform/consent-mirror, which sits in the platform-key group (the
same shared-secret guard as workspace provisioning).

