THE MODIFICATION (2026-10-28, part 9) — `lifecycle_stage`, and `lead_source` as an origin
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Added: `lifecycle_stage`, a DERIVED people select (lead / opportunity / customer /
lost) folded over a contact's opportunities, its writers and its corrective
schedule; a read-only guard on it; and `lead_source` rewritten to record where a
contact came from rather than which channel it arrived on.

Reason: the pipeline already knew the answer (the deals), and every surface that
needed "where is this person in the funnel" was re-deriving it from the
opportunity table with its own rule. The fold exists in exactly one class here
(App\Support\LifecycleStage\LifecycleStage) and both writers call it, so the CRM
board, the API and the platform's attribution read the same answer. `lead_source`
had been carrying channel names (LINE, WhatsApp, Web widget), which duplicated
`preferred_channel` and could not answer the question its name asks.

