Going from a running container to its source, without asking anyone:

  $ docker inspect marketing-platform-relaticle-1 --format '{{.Config.Image}}'
  ghcr.io/pthk100/relaticle-platform:3.6.3-lifecycle-stage
  $ git clone https://github.com/pthk100/relaticle.git
  $ git -C relaticle show a1e8338fb --stat
  $ git -C relaticle checkout a1e8338fb && docker build -t relaticle-local .

The tags are HOST-LOCAL: each was built with `docker build` on the dev host and
has never been pushed, because no registry credential for `pthk100` exists on that
host or on the build workstation (`docker push` answers "unauthorized"). The image
tag is therefore a name for a local image id, not a published artefact, and this
repository at the commit above is the whole of the §13 source offer for it. The
image's own contents are the tree at that commit; the Dockerfile in it rebuilds the
same application.

